From a7e44e2a8437fe4d55ef1be271d758269fc328d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:52:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] upkg: the add-on rows come from upkg_rows, one parser
 for the curses browse and the Workbench window

upkg browse parsed the four lists (list, list-installed, list-upgradable, list-new)
and ran install, remove and upgrade inside its curses code. Both move to
libopkg/upkg_rows.c, which has no curses and no Intuition: upkg_rows_load builds
{name, kind, installed, available, description} rows, upkg_rows_run runs the
command through opkg_cmd_exec with an optional output sink, rebuilds the package
hash and loads the rows again. upkg browse keeps only the menu text and colours.
